how are you doing sir  hey how lovely to see you nice to see  you  um i'm gonna start with oh sorry what  even in this crazy world  100 zoom 100 um  i have a lot of fun with this movie uh  it is  literally non-stop action like beginning  to end it slows down a few times but  it's a lot of action  um how did you pull this off the amount  of action  you have with obviously the budget you  you obviously never have enough budget  but how did you do this we prepped for a  long time so everything was kind of  meticulously planned  and um and then i think one of the keys  to kind of make the movie look as big as  it is  is we went to real locations to shoot it  you know i think when you try and make a  movie like this there are two ways of  doing it one is to  stay in a studio backlot situation put  up a big green screen shoot against the  green screen and then create the  environment  in the computer i didn't want to take  that route because i felt  it would make the movie feel a little  kind of synthetic  i knew the monsters had to be cg so i  thought everything else in the movie  should be as real as we could possibly  make it  and uh so we went to these insanely  remote  real epic looking locations and shot the  movie for real  and then inserted the creatures into  those plates that we'd shot  and i think we got not not just insane  production value but also an insane look  for the movie  by going to these remote locations and  shooting for real  and quite often a lot of these locations  were places that had never been put on  camera  before which is really exciting for me  as a filmmaker because he's so used to  going to places where other people have  shot  already to be able to go and shoot  something fresh and exciting  to create this brand new world was you  know was thrilling for me  but it was tough you know we we had to  take the whole cast and crew 350 people  and have them live in tent villages kind  of hundreds of miles away from the  nearest habitation  we put in roads we'd have to kind of dig  wells for water  um it was real kind of uh extreme  gorilla film making  but i think the you know the look we got  is pretty exceptional and pretty unique  at what day of the shoot did you realize  shooting in a desert  sucks ah day one  it didn't take very long um for a whole  bunch of reasons you know it's uh  it's hot i don't know if anyone ever  told you that but it's hot in the desert  and so for the for the actors especially  tony he's wearing all this  fur trimming on his outfits and like the  the costumes are very hot so it was very  unpleasant for the actors  and then of course they're doing all  this complex fight choreography  and um they're having to do it in sand  and as anyone who's tried to run in the  sand nose it's like five times as  difficult as  kind of trying to do a fight scene when  you're on a just a level flat  floor um so it it made everything  difficult  and then you know we'd be living in  tents and as hot as it was during the  day  you'd go back to your tent as soon as  the sun went down it will be below zero  and then generally these big storms  would come up they'd blow the tents away  or they'd knock over the windmill that  was providing the water from the well  so there'd be no water i mean it was uh  it was it was hard filmmaking  but um but i but it was very exciting at  the same time  and also for the actors it kind of put  them in  in the mindset that they were in this  new fantastic world  it felt like a kind of difficult  dangerous world they were in  because they were actually as actors  physically living it you know they  weren't kind of having to  to pretend it in front of the green  screen and then go back to their hotel  room at the four seasons  completely um i have not played the game  but i do know that the cat  uh that's on the ship is a really big  deal um  and so talk a little bit about the  importance of putting that character  in the movie and uh you know for fans of  the  of the of the video games i know it's a  big deal  well i think um i'm glad you really  enjoyed the movie and you know nothing  about the video game because that's what  we've tried to do is fashion a movie  that  absolutely works if you have no  knowledge of the game you can still come  and really enjoy  a great action adventure movie with  giant monsters  and but if you know the game the movie  is loaded with fine detail  um that that really brings the game to  life  all of the characters that mila meets  are characters from the video game  and their costumes are exactly correct  the locations are exactly correct the  monsters are exactly as they are in the  game  and most of all the palakko the chef  character that you meet  is taken directly from the game and we  consulted with the game  um makers uh the creators of the game to  actually get every  every bit of detail about him right um i  had several sessions trying to get the  pitch of his voice correct  because originally the game creator said  no no it's too high pitched then it was  too low pitched  and eventually just like the baby bears  porridge it was just right  we tried to really please um the  creators of the game because i felt they  were the gatekeepers to this property  and if  if they were happy then the fans of the  game would also be happy  i don't want to get specific with any  spoilers but i think  one of the things that i really enjoyed  was there were some twists and turns  that happened in the movie that i  absolutely did not expect um  and i don't even want to say where and  when because it will ruin things  but uh talk a little bit about sort of  not  how can i say this about um i don't  think the audience is expecting some of  the stuff that's going to happen in the  movie  well i think you know genre audiences  are the smartest audiences on the planet  i mean  and because they they they consume  movies they consume genre  they can generally be ahead of the movie  because they kind of know all the  conventions  so they kind of know where stories are  generally headed  um i shed my 13 year old daughter  inception the other day  and it was incredible because i remember  film critics being baffled by the plot  of inception some for some people it was  too complicated 10 years ago right  my 13 year old watched the first 15  minutes and then said daddy  i think this is what's going to happen  and she pitched me the entire movie she  knew nothing about it didn't even know  who leonardo dicaprio was  um so so she's smart because she watches  genre movies she kind of had anticipated  what it was going to be  so i've always seen it as my job as a  genre filmmaker to try and kind of  kind of take the audience by surprise  and kind of throw in something that  you're just not expecting  you think you know where the movie is  going to go and then it goes in a  completely different direction  and i think if you can achieve that with  a genre audience then you've really  you've really done your job as a  director  obviously why i'm curious you've made it  with resident evil there were a lot of  sequels  with this um is there thought in your  brain of if this is successful  doing more is it something that you're  really interested in i i  love the world of the game i became  involved in it 12 years ago when i  played the game for the first time in  japan  um when when really no one outside of  japan had  knew what monster hunter was it was kind  of a japanese-only phenomena  um and it's a you know it's a game  that's been going for 15 years so it's  obviously built a vast world  only part of which you can kind of um  put on screen in any one movie  so you know it definitely it's a world i  would love to return to but for me you  know i've always tried to stay focused  on one movie at a time  i think every movie has to function as a  self-contained unit  and and that's what this movie does it  tells um it tells  i think a very strong story with some  great character  work between mila and tony and a very  satisfying story  and then you know if audiences want more  then absolutely it's a world i would  love to delve back into  on that note i gotta go um seriously i  had a lot of fun with it man  i hope i hope it's a big hit for you  guys thank you so much

